Subject: [PATCH 3/3] pymalloc blocks as Sublet child lifetimes (CDERIVE/CREVOKE)
Upstream: CPython 3.13.7
Upstream-Archive: https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.7/Python-3.13.7.tgz
Upstream-SHA256: 6c9d80839cfa20024f34d9a6dd31ae2a9cd97ff5e980e969209746037a5153b2
Build-Variants: Capstone application, PYMALLOC_SUBLET=ON (prepare-source.py --variant protected)
Depends-On: cpython-3.13.7-0002-capability-provenance.patch
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

The protection is two instructions where obmalloc hands a block out and takes
it back (capstone/docs/design/virtual-capstone/isa.md); the interpreter's
patch 0014 makes the same changes in the full tree:

- new_arena derives a child of the arena (arena_life, carrying MANAGE), at
  the arena's own address within the capability the arena allocator
  returned.
- pymalloc_alloc returns a child of arena_life bounded to the request.
- pymalloc_free revokes that child, which faults on a reference that is not
  a live block of this arena, and continues with obmalloc's own pointer.
  POOL_ADDR (0002) resolves the pool by address, so no client pointer is
  dereferenced.
- pymalloc_realloc replaces the client's child when the block stays, and
  copies only the issued length when it moves.

